    },
    {
      "unresolved": false,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "ca8da184_72c92103",
        "filename": "tests/cts/hostside/app/src/com/android/cts/net/hostside/NetworkPolicyManagerTest.java",
        "patchSetId": 4
      },
      "lineNbr": 61,
      "author": {
        "id": 1308163
      },
      "writtenOn": "2021-06-18T23:07:55Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "I just found that if the network is non-metered, then assertBackgroundNetworkAccess(false) will fail because in checkNetworkStatus() it will call getActiveNetworkInfo()(which will call isUidNetworkingBlocked() indirectly) and if the network is non-metered, the isUidNetworkingBlocked() will return false and the state of NetworkInfo will be CONNECTED.\nI think the problem is that when power saver mode is enabled(for example), NetworkPolicy needs some time to update the uid rule, so if isUidNetworkingBlocked() is called before the uid rule has updated, then the return value of isUidNetworkingBlocked() might be wrong.\n\nI replaced assertBackgroundNetworkAccess() with isUidNetworkingBlockedWithRetry() to make sure the uid rules has updated correctly.",
      "parentUuid": "a23823c8_3e775856",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 61,
        "startChar": 8,
        "endLine": 61,
        "endChar": 68
      },
      "revId": "8d86619fb9a64cbeee393f363f670e0da5344149",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "af67d29b_4532bc07",
        "filename": "tests/cts/hostside/app/src/com/android/cts/net/hostside/NetworkPolicyManagerTest.java",
